comments[12]:
  - created_at: "2026-08-03T20:56:39.512Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "A clean natural experiment, observed 2026-08-03 immediately after this item was filed.\n\nA commit touching only tracker data under the pm store, with no source, script, workflow or test file changed, turned the Windows regression job on main red. Two tests in the init command suite failed at 30010 and 30002 milliseconds, which is the generic Vitest timeout rather than an assertion. Re-running the failed job against byte-identical content passed, and main is green at the same commit.\n\nThe experiment is clean because the input could not have caused a behavioural change. Tracker data is not read by that suite, which sandboxes its own store path. So the failure carried zero information about the commit and the leg still reported red.\n\nTwo consequences for this item.\n\nFirst, the measured failure rate is a mixture and nothing separates its parts. Of the 28 alerts counted here, an unknown fraction are product defects that a pre-merge control would have caught, and an unknown fraction are infrastructure timeouts that no control can catch because there is nothing to catch. A rate that mixes them cannot justify any decision, which strengthens rather than weakens the case for measuring it properly: the first thing the meter has to do is partition.\n\nSecond, the timeout class is itself a recurrence. Two items in this tracker are already closed for the same subject, Windows init package acceptance exceeding the generic Vitest timeout, and both closed with a per-site timeout increase. The class has returned on a third site. That is the second independent recurrence found today and it arrived, unprompted, in the CI response to the commit that filed the recurrence work.\n\nPartitioning rule this suggests, recorded as input rather than as a decision: a failure whose signature is a timeout at the declared limit, on a leg whose median passing duration for that suite is far below the limit, and which passes on re-run with identical content, is infrastructure. Everything else is a candidate defect until proved otherwise. The re-run is the discriminator and it is cheap.\n"
  - created_at: "2026-10-03T12:05:39.807Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Fresh all-status intake: the strict corpus contains 2866 readable items, no omissions and only the three active receipt-correction owners in progress. Reuse this canonical nightly recurrence family rather than creating four duplicate occurrence items. Scheduled Nightly Validation run 37114037678 at ca6e718707d7a1582f7abc437f5bd88aab156dfd raised GH-1377 (Windows Node24 shard1: preview-snapshot invalid-lookup expected native ENOENT, received transaction_preview_snapshot_changed), GH-1378 (Windows Node24 shard2: search query cursor fingerprint mismatch plus settings entry/open race expectations), GH-1379 (Ubuntu Node22: three linked workspace-snapshot cases raise ENOENT during stat of dangling aliases), and GH-1380 (macOS Node24: settings entry/open race fallback and permission/link expectations). The Ubuntu Node24 coverage, independent quality and Ubuntu Node25 jobs passed; the four platform legs failed. These are real pre-existing-main observations distinct from PR1376 checks and source coverage. Historical shipped source lineages pm-5iwfkj, pm-gh1370 and pm-j668gl remain completed under their recorded boundaries; this recurrence intake records new platform investigation evidence, without claiming a repair or assigning inactive roadmap work. Each GitHub alert receives this canonical PM-file link and remains open pending independent platform repair proof."
    edited_at: "2026-10-03T12:20:41.253Z"
  - created_at: "2026-10-03T13:54:16.058Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Additional reproducible verification observation: full local Node26/npm12 coverage twice reached the packed SDK continuation test and exceeded its unchanged 30-second npm-pack subprocess deadline. Its unchanged isolated control passed all11 real public SDK traversal scenarios; clean packed Node/Bun manual acceptance and the nine-package npx/bunx clean-consumer gate also passed. This is an environment/scheduling candidate, not a proven package defect or established root cause. The whole suite is being rerun on the CI-supported Node24.12/npm11 profile with no deadline, assertion, denominator or threshold changes. Existing Windows/macOS/Node22 nightly portability alerts still require their own repairs; neither this observation nor the isolated pass closes them. Historical shipped continuation implementation remains closed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-03T14:33:21.732Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Concrete Node22 snapshot occurrence now has a verified local compatibility repair under its existing linked snapshot owner in PR1376. The existing GH1379 canonical-link comment was updated in place to include that owner and unchanged ten-case cross-runtime proof, without a duplicate comment or PM item. The other platform occurrences remain pending, and this family stays open/unclaimed until their actual repair and hosted verification."
  - created_at: "2026-10-05T11:59:59.622Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Scheduled run 37301905006 at main 7077aca produced GH1409 and GH1410 with the same portable-backup get exit4 on Windows/macOS. Distinct causal child pm-gh1409 now owns the SDK source-spelling fix, real Linux red/green status assertion and required native acceptance in PR1402. This recurrence measurement family stays open and unclaimed; no shipped predecessor is reopened or release history reassigned."
  - created_at: "2026-10-09T19:52:08.293Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Implementation scope: original GitHub first attempts, per-leg SDK recurrence evaluation, complete paginated all-state alert evidence, explicit unknown cause classification, UTC affected days and censored alert-closure latency. Derive current leg population from the actual workflow and preserve historical observed legs. Enforce declared failure/coverage thresholds in a separately persisted operational report; closure never rewrites the original failure denominator."
  - created_at: "2026-10-09T20:05:09.344Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Test-audit evidence: the public SDK suite owns recurrence semantics; the collector suite independently proves GitHub pagination, original attempt identity, legacy leg retention, PM-link correlation and trusted workflow routing. Only external GitHub transport is substituted. The pre-fix timestamp and mixed-open-alert regressions failed independently, then the implementation was corrected. No coverage denominator, threshold or suppression changed. The first broad static run detected 121 tests in a 120-file SDK directory; the new governance test now lives under tests/unit/sdk/governance rather than relaxing the organization gate."
  - created_at: "2026-10-09T20:13:23.232Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Live historical reconciliation: all 28 alert issues created 2026-06-20 through 2026-08-03 retain original-run references and canonical PM repair links. The caller-chosen 45-day report ending 2026-08-04 retains the original red jobs and clean Ubuntu Node25/Node20 negative controls. Complete live metadata and histories of all 22 unique recorded repair owners were downloaded with no omissions. Added only evidenced discovered_from relationships to this measurement owner; source repairs remain closed. The original issue description grouped four Windows Node20 alerts under Windows Node24; live titles preserve those runtime generations separately. Alert counts and red-job occurrences are different populations: an issue can contain subsequent failed runs in comments."
  - created_at: "2026-10-09T20:30:50.621Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Verification checkpoint: the first full Node24 run passed all 10023 behavioral tests and two legitimate Windows-only skips, while the unchanged exact coverage gate rejected one unexercised multi-origin ordering callback. The origin partition regression now asserts an independent chronological ID sequence including same-instant tie breaking. The broad source suite is being rerun without coverage exclusions or threshold changes. An overlapping linked run timed out waiting for the build lease; after the suite released that lease, the same linked command passed unchanged. Run broad and linked builds sequentially to avoid manufacturing a harness timeout."
  - created_at: "2026-10-09T20:47:37.956Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Completed implementation evidence: public SDK windows, first-attempt collector, all-state alert/PM correlation, stable alert-owner comments and enforced per-leg workflow policy pass 76 focused cases and the full 10023-test suite at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. A final live production-collector replay ending 2026-08-04 retains 280 original family observations, all 28 linked historical alerts and genuine healthy zero-rate Ubuntu/macOS legacy legs. The live 30-day meter faithfully remains red for macOS and both Windows shards at the unchanged 10% policy; this resolves missing measurement rather than erasing outcomes. Packed Node24/Node26/Bun, strict typed consumers, nine-package npx/bunx acceptance and 91-step package-first dogfood with real local semantic indexing/hybrid search passed. Publication of this reviewed source is a separate future daily release claim."
  - created_at: "2026-10-09T21:10:26.166Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "PR1432 review triage: the synthetic old-run pending finding is confirmed and will use workflow definitions at each original head SHA. The rejected-search finding is disproved by a fresh authenticated GitHub search returning total_count=20 and incomplete_results=false with the exact RFC3339 updated qualifier; GitHub documentation permits time precision. Shared issue closure is the explicitly selected alert-closure latency endpoint, not verified per-attempt product repair; original outcomes and unknown causes remain unchanged. A reused-episode regression will preserve that distinction. Hosted exact source checks passed, and current telemetry client successful flush plus healthy ingestion services and an empty broker queue are observed, without claiming permanent drainage or exhaustive per-action tracing."
  - created_at: "2026-10-09T21:47:01.576Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review-corrected evidence: original-head workflow populations retain 230 genuine observations, all 28 historical alert issues and 45 distinct workflow SHAs in the 45-day replay ending 2026-08-04. The earlier 280-row receipt remains in immutable history; its synthetic current-family pending rows are superseded by this corrected census. Legacy healthy zero-rate controls remain genuine, and newly added current families have no fabricated historical attempts. The unchanged linked SDK/collector command passes 62 cases. A reused-alert regression preserves two failures with unknown causes and shared alert-closure latencies of 60 and 120 minutes; those endpoints are not verified product-repair dates."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-09T20:13:24.004Z","harness:codex","A reliability denominator must count original job attempts, not alert issues. Reused alert comments can carry several occurrences; closure is only an observed latency endpoint and never rewrites the original outcome or supplies an inferred product/infrastructure cause."
  "2026-10-09T21:47:02.106Z","harness:codex","Historical populations are versioned evidence: read each original run workflow at its immutable SHA and cache repeated definitions within one census. The current matrix cannot supply absent historical attempts, and closure-only alert latency must remain explicitly separate from verified product repair."
